meta {
  name: provider registry rows
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/providers
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  One row per provider the config knows: kind, state (needs-key, needs-download, configured, reachable, failed), keyPresent as a boolean, endpoint, models, live, reason and checkedAt. Sends no request to any provider; it shows presence plus the answer of the last check.
  
  Fence: host. Loopback fence: the TCP peer must be loopback AND the Host header must be localhost/127.0.0.1/::1. A REST client passes automatically when it targets http://localhost:<port>. A LAN IP or rebound DNS name in the URL answers a blank 404.
  
  Writes state: no
}
